From 73d0f2240b7d330725adc66c2edb6c5330ab8398 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kamalbuilds <geniusamansingh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:50:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix: install @solidcash packages without git, with a check
 that fails when they do not

Every published @solidcash package that uses libauth (utils, solidc, solidcash, testing, and solidhat
through solidcash) declared it as git+https://github.com/mainnet-pat/libauth.git#1cf4b432. npm
refuses that spec under allow-git=none (EALLOWGIT), and so does any CI image or container without
git or ssh keys, so `npm install @solidcash/solidcash` failed there.

Point the dependency at the same commit's GitHub archive tarball instead: a remote tarball is not a
git dependency, and the commit already carries the prebuilt build/ tree, so nothing has to run on
install. The root resolution, yarn.lock and the example manifests follow.

scripts/check-installable-without-git.mjs packs every release package, installs the tarballs into an
empty project with --allow-git=none and loads libauth from each. EXTRA_TARBALLS installs companion
packages alongside, for @mem-cash/*, which declares the same git spec in its own repository.
